# Shared packages (`@questorylabs/shared`, `@questorylabs/ui`, `@questorylabs/db`)

## Zod schemas

- Pattern: `export const XSchema = z.object({...})` + `export type X = z.infer<typeof XSchema>`.
- `packages/shared/src/index.ts` is already a 1500+ line barrel. Do not keep appending: new domains or large schema groups go in their own file (like `pagination.ts` / `safe-href.ts`) and are re-exported from the index.
- Any request/response contract consumed by both `apps/api` and `apps/web` belongs here — not in `apps/web/src/lib` (the enterprise types stranded in `apps/web/src/lib/enterprise-types.ts` are the anti-pattern).

## Server-only code

Session and OAuth crypto stay in the `@questorylabs/shared/session` and `@questorylabs/shared/oauth-state` subpath exports. Never re-export them (or any Node-only code) from the browser-safe barrel `src/index.ts`.

## UI (`packages/ui`, `@questorylabs/ui`)

Generic React primitives and design tokens live here (`Button`, `Dialog`, `PageHeader`, `Panel`, `EmptyState`, `Skeleton*`, `HatchShadow`, `styles.css`). The package is consumed as source — Next apps must set `transpilePackages: ["@questorylabs/ui"]` and `@import "@questorylabs/ui/styles.css"`.

- New generic UI goes in `packages/ui` with a colocated `*.spec.tsx`. Variant styling uses `cva` + `cn` (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`); export the recipe (`buttonVariants`) next to the component. Do not hand-roll `Record<Variant, string>` maps.
- Product-only chrome stays in the app (`QMark`, `StateMessage`, gates, domain views).
- `apps/web/src/components/ui` re-exports this package so existing `@/components/ui` imports keep working.

## Prisma (`packages/db`)

- Edit only `packages/db/prisma/schema.template.prisma`. The generated `schema.prisma` and Prisma client are build artifacts (`pnpm db:schema` / `db:generate`) — never edit or commit them, never fork per-app schemas.
- After schema changes, run `pnpm db:schema && pnpm db:generate` so `apps/api` picks up the regenerated client.

## Tests

Every exported helper/schema/component gets a colocated `*.spec.ts(x)` (see `session.spec.ts`, `pagination.spec.ts`, `Button.spec.tsx`). Run with `pnpm --filter @questorylabs/shared test` or `pnpm --filter @questorylabs/ui test`.
